2. Create a program with Parent class as Person and 2 child class Student,Employee. The Person class should have method Studying(), Working(). Inherit the child classes as per the appropriate methods.


class Person {
	void studing() {
		System.out.println("Person is studing");
	}
	
	void working() {
		System.out.println("Person is working");
	}
	
}

class Student extends Person {
	void studentDetails() {
		System.out.println("This person is student");
	}
}

class Employee extends Person {
	void employeeDetails() {
		System.out.println("This person is an employee");
	}
}

public class InheritanceAssing {

	public static void main(String[] args) {

		Student std = new Student();
		std.studentDetails();
		std.studing();
		
		Employee emp = new Employee();
		emp.employeeDetails();
		emp.working();
	}

}

Output :

This person is student
Person is studing
This person is an employee
Person is working

